{"item_uid": "指考99-english-022", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 37, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Why did the Mint issue the US $1 coins?", "options": {"A": "In response to U.S. citizens’ requests.", "B": "In memory of the late U.S. presidents.", "C": "To attract more train commuters.", "D": "To promote the trading of dollar bills."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "B", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 5.0, "B": 77.0, "C": 3.0, "D": 8.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 1.0, "B": 97.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 10.0, "B": 50.0, "C": 8.0, "D": 16.0}, "omit_rate": 8.0, "p_value": 77.0, "p_high": 97.0, "p_low": 50.0, "discrimination": 47.0, "p_quintiles": [98.0, 93.0, 85.0, 67.0, 41.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-023", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 38, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "What may you find on the heads side of the new US $1 coin?", "options": {"A": "The name of a U.S. president.", "B": "The year when the coin was made.", "C": "The Statue of Liberty.", "D": "English proverbs."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "A", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 73.0, "B": 7.0, "C": 13.0, "D": 3.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 93.0, "B": 2.0, "C": 4.0, "D": 1.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 46.0, "B": 14.0, "C": 24.0, "D": 5.0}, "omit_rate": 5.0, "p_value": 73.0, "p_high": 93.0, "p_low": 46.0, "discrimination": 47.0, "p_quintiles": [95.0, 88.0, 79.0, 64.0, 37.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-024", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 39, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred about the presidential coins?", "options": {"A": "President Gerald Ford’s coin was issued in 2008.", "B": "The U.S. Mint has issued all the presidential coins by now.", "C": "No presidential coin has been released for President Barack Obama.", "D": "Every U.S. president had his coin made two years after his term was over.\n第第第第 40 至至至至 43 題題題題為為為為題題題題組組組組\nNewspapers have tried many things to stop a seemingly nonstop decline in readers. Now France is\npushing forward with a novel approach: giving away papers to young readers in an effort to turn them\ninto regular customers. The French government recently detailed plans of a project called “My Free\nNewspaper,” under which 18- to 24-year-olds will be offered a free, year-long subscription to a\nnewspaper of their choice.\n- 4 -\n第 5 頁 99年指考\n共 7 頁 英文考科\nNewspaper readership in France has been especially low among young people. According to a\ngovernment study, only 10 percent of those aged 15 to 24 read a paid-for newspaper daily in 2007, down\nfrom 20 percent a decade earlier.\nEmmanuel Schwartzenberg, a former media editor of Le Figaro, the oldest and second-largest\nnational newspaper in France, said he had strong reservations about the government project. At a time\nwhen advertising is in steep decline, he said, newspapers should instead be looking at ways to raise more\nprofits from readers, rather than giving papers away. “This just reinforces the belief that newspapers\nshould be free, which is a very bad idea,” Mr. Schwartzenberg said.\nFrench readers, young and old, already have plenty of free options from which to choose, including\nnewspaper websites and the free papers handed out daily in many city centers. Some bloggers said the\nnew program might hold the most appeal to the few young people who do already read, and buy,\nnewspapers.\nThe French government plans to promote the program with an advertising campaign aimed at young\nreaders and their parents. However, when asked how to attract young readers to the printed press, the\ngovernment said the primary channel for the ads would be the Internet."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "C", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 4.0, "B": 9.0, "C": 62.0, "D": 14.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 1.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 93.0, "D": 4.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 7.0, "B": 20.0, "C": 26.0, "D": 25.0}, "omit_rate": 11.0, "p_value": 62.0, "p_high": 93.0, "p_low": 26.0, "discrimination": 67.0, "p_quintiles": [96.0, 86.0, 68.0, 41.0, 20.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-025", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 40, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Why did the French government decide to launch the free newspaper program?", "options": {"A": "To fight economic recession.", "B": "To win approval from youngsters.", "C": "To promote newspaper readership.", "D": "To improve the literacy rate in France."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "C", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 2.0, "B": 20.0, "C": 65.0, "D": 8.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 0.0, "B": 9.0, "C": 88.0, "D": 2.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 5.0, "B": 29.0, "C": 40.0, "D": 14.0}, "omit_rate": 5.0, "p_value": 65.0, "p_high": 88.0, "p_low": 40.0, "discrimination": 48.0, "p_quintiles": [92.0, 80.0, 65.0, 51.0, 35.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-026", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 41, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be concluded from the passage?", "options": {"A": "Everyone considers the government project creative.", "B": "Newspaper readership is much higher in other countries.", "C": "Research shows young people have no interest in current affairs.", "D": "Giving away free papers is not a strong enough incentive to attract readers."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "D", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 5.0, "B": 7.0, "C": 20.0, "D": 56.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 1.0, "B": 2.0, "C": 11.0, "D": 85.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 11.0, "B": 15.0, "C": 26.0, "D": 26.0}, "omit_rate": 12.0, "p_value": 56.0, "p_high": 85.0, "p_low": 26.0, "discrimination": 59.0, "p_quintiles": [89.0, 75.0, 58.0, 39.0, 20.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-027", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 42, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "What is Mr. Schwartzenberg’s attitude toward this program?", "options": {"A": "Skeptical.", "B": "Devoted.", "C": "Optimistic.", "D": "Indifferent."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "A", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 39.0, "B": 16.0, "C": 14.0, "D": 19.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 68.0, "B": 10.0, "C": 5.0, "D": 15.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 15.0, "B": 20.0, "C": 23.0, "D": 20.0}, "omit_rate": 12.0, "p_value": 39.0, "p_high": 68.0, "p_low": 14.0, "discrimination": 54.0, "p_quintiles": [77.0, 51.0, 33.0, 19.0, 13.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-028", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 43, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "According to the passage, where would the information about the free newspaper program in France\nmost likely be seen?", "options": {"A": "In magazines.", "B": "On blogs.", "C": "In newspapers.", "D": "On the Internet.\n第第第第 44 至至至至 47 題題題題為為為為題題題題組組組組\nCoffee experts are willing to pay large sums of money for high-quality coffee beans. The high-end\nbeans, such as Kona or Blue Mountain, are known to cost extraordinary sums of money. Then there is\nKopi Lowak (translated as “Civet Coffee”), the world’s most expensive coffee, which sells for as much as\nUS $50 per quarter-pound.\nThis isn’t particularly surprising, given that approximately 500 pounds a year of Kopi Lowak\nconstitute the entire world supply. What is surprising is why this particular coffee is so rare. In fact, it’s\nnot the plants that are rare. It’s the civet droppings. That’s right, the civet droppings—the body waste of\nthe palm civet. Coffee beans aren’t Kopi Lowak until they’ve been digested and come out in the body\nwaste of the palm civet.\nPalm civets are tree-dwelling, raccoon-like little animals, native to Southeast Asia and the\nIndonesian islands. They also have a love for coffee cherries. According to Kopi Lowak suppliers, palm\ncivets eat the fruit whole, but only digest the outer fruit, leaving the beans intact. While the beans are not\n- 5 -\n99年指考 第 6 頁\n英文考科 共 7 頁\ndestroyed, they undergo a transformation in the animal’s body. A chemical substance in the digestive\nsystem of the palm civet causes some changes to the beans to give them a unique flavor. However, this is\nnot the only explanation why coffee beans retrieved from civet droppings have a special flavor all their\nown. Another possible reason is that palm civets have an unfailing instinct for picking the coffee cherries\nat the peak of their ripeness.\nKopi Lowak is reported to have a character in taste unlike any other coffee, complex with caramel\nundertones and an earthy or gamey flavor. Currently, most of the world’s supply of Kopi Lowak is sold in\nJapan, though a few US markets are also starting to stock up on Kopi Lowak."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "D", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 3.0, "B": 5.0, "C": 9.0, "D": 79.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 1.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 3.0, "D": 95.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 6.0, "B": 10.0, "C": 18.0, "D": 57.0}, "omit_rate": 5.0, "p_value": 79.0, "p_high": 95.0, "p_low": 57.0, "discrimination": 38.0, "p_quintiles": [96.0, 92.0, 86.0, 76.0, 46.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-029", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 44, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "What does “This” in the second paragraph refer to?", "options": {"A": "Civet Coffee.", "B": "Blue Mountain coffee.", "C": "The high price of Kopi Lowak.", "D": "The unique taste of Kona."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "C", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 14.0, "B": 3.0, "C": 77.0, "D": 2.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 2.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 97.0, "D": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 28.0, "B": 8.0, "C": 49.0, "D": 5.0}, "omit_rate": 4.0, "p_value": 77.0, "p_high": 97.0, "p_low": 49.0, "discrimination": 48.0, "p_quintiles": [99.0, 95.0, 86.0, 68.0, 39.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-030", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 45, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Why is Kopi Lowak expensive?", "options": {"A": "There is a very limited supply of the beans.", "B": "The coffee trees that grow the beans are scarce.", "C": "It takes a long time for the coffee beans to ripen.", "D": "Only a few experts know how to produce the beans."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "A", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 51.0, "B": 9.0, "C": 26.0, "D": 6.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 75.0, "B": 2.0, "C": 21.0, "D": 2.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 27.0, "B": 18.0, "C": 26.0, "D": 13.0}, "omit_rate": 8.0, "p_value": 51.0, "p_high": 75.0, "p_low": 27.0, "discrimination": 48.0, "p_quintiles": [82.0, 61.0, 50.0, 40.0, 21.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-031", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 46, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "What is the main point discussed in the third paragraph?", "options": {"A": "Why palm civets like the coffee beans.", "B": "Where Kopi Lowak is mainly harvested.", "C": "What chemicals are found in the civet’s digestive system.", "D": "How palm civets change coffee fruit to Kopi Lowak beans."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "D", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 5.0, "B": 6.0, "C": 12.0, "D": 66.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 1.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 2.0, "D": 96.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 10.0, "B": 13.0, "C": 22.0, "D": 33.0}, "omit_rate": 10.0, "p_value": 66.0, "p_high": 96.0, "p_low": 33.0, "discrimination": 63.0, "p_quintiles": [98.0, 90.0, 71.0, 47.0, 27.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-032", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 47, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements is true, according to the passage?", "options": {"A": "Little palm civets eat only the outer layer of the coffee cherries.", "B": "Palm civets somehow know the right time when the coffee fruit ripens.", "C": "Kopi Lowak is most popular in Southeast Asia and the Indonesian islands.", "D": "Kona and Blue Mountain are the most expensive coffees but only of average quality.\n第第第第 48 至至至至 51 題題題題為為為為題題題題組組組組\nGunter Grass was the winner of the 1999 Nobel Prize in Literature. His talents are revealed in a\nvariety of disciplines: He is not only a novelist, poet and playwright, but also a renowned painter and\nsculptor. As he himself stresses, his creations are closely related to his unique personal history. His father\nwas a German who joined the Nazi party in World War II, while his mother was Polish. As a result, he\nconstantly suffered contradictory feelings: as a Pole who had been victimized, and as someone guilty of\nharming the Poles. The torment in his heart led him to denounce the Nazis and his political activism has\ncontinued throughout his career. His commitment to the peace movement and the environmental\nmovement as well as his unfailing quest for justice has won him praise as “the conscience of the nation.”\nIn the spring of 1996, he was inspired during a trip to Italy to write a poem with his watercolor brush\ndirectly on one of his paintings. Before long, a collection of his “water poems” was born. Painting and\nliterature have become his major forms of creativity. For him, painting is a form of creation with concrete,\nsensual elements, while writing is a hard and abstract process. When he cannot find words to convey his\nthoughts, painting helps him find the words to express himself. In this way, Grass not only creates simple\ndepictions of the objects he is fond of in life, such as melons, vegetables, fish, and mushrooms, but also\nuses them as symbols for mental associations of various kinds. For example, to express the complexity of\nreality, he sometimes places unrelated objects in the same painting, such as a bird and a housefly, or a\n- 6 -\n第 7 頁 99年指考\n共 7 頁 英文考科\nmushroom and a nail. Grass has depicted a wide variety of natural scenes, animals and plants, and even\nhuman artifacts of the German countryside, portraying them in poems, and allowing words to make the\npaintings rich in literary value."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "B", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 19.0, "B": 47.0, "C": 11.0, "D": 7.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 16.0, "B": 75.0, "C": 5.0, "D": 2.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 16.0, "B": 24.0, "C": 19.0, "D": 13.0}, "omit_rate": 16.0, "p_value": 47.0, "p_high": 75.0, "p_low": 24.0, "discrimination": 51.0, "p_quintiles": [85.0, 58.0, 39.0, 30.0, 21.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考99-english-033", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 99, "year_ce": 2010, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 48, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "What caused Grass to feel confused and troubled when he was young?", "options": {"A": "He was the son of a Nazi and a victimized Pole.", "B": "He found himself fighting two opposing political parties.", "C": "He was trained to be an artist though he wanted to be a poet.", "D": "He was born with so many talents that he couldn’t choose a direction."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "A", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 63.0, "B": 11.0, "C": 6.0, "D": 5.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 94.0, "B": 5.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 26.0, "B": 16.0, "C": 15.0, "D": 12.0}, "omit_rate": 15.0, "p_value": 63.0, "p_high": 94.0, "p_low": 26.0, "discrimination": 68.0, "p_quintiles": [97.0, 87.0, 68.0, 43.0, 19.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
